s":[0,0,0,0.0],"guidance":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.029,"r5":0.0526,"r20":0.1446,"r1_spy":0.0122,"r5_spy":-0.0027,"r20_spy":0.0944,"r1_sector":-0.026,"r5_sector":-0.0635,"r20_sector":0.0469,"etf":"XLK"}}],"quotes":[{"c":"PTC 2020 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2020-01-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"And just highlighting we put it in the prepared remarks, but when we put out the initial restructuring estimate for the year that was based on an estimate -- current estimates actually have that about $5 million higher.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2020 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2020-01-22","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"For fiscal '20, we're increasing our guidance to a range of $1.27 billion to $1.29 billion or 14% to 16% year-over-year growth and 13% to 15% on a constant currency basis.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2020 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2020-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"I am referring to our business model transition, our successful expansion into high growth IoT and AR markets, our recent embrace of a pure SaaS future through the Onshape acquisition and the restructuring we did earlier this year before the pandemic arrived.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2020 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2020-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"The last change I want to talk about is restructuring and cost management.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2020 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"For the full year, free cash flow guidance includes $45 million in restructuring costs, $9 million of acquisition related payments, $65 million of interest payments and CapEx investments in the low to 20 - low to mid $20 million range.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2020 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"…decrease roughly $25 million compared to fiscal ’20, given our new debt structure, and assuming no restructuring, we would expect $30 million less of restructuring payments and assuming no acquisitions, another approximately $10 million less of actual acquisition related payments in fiscal ‘21.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2020 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2020-10-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Note that free cash flow for the year includes approximately $52 million of restructuring and acquisition-related payments, as well as approximately $8 million of incremental interest paid before we retire the $500 million of 6% notes back in May.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2020 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2020-10-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"As we've said previously, fiscal 2021 free cash flow growth benefits from reduced interest, restructuring and acquisition-related payments.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2021-01-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Heppelmann","x":"They are adopting Onshape to streamline communication between mechanical designers, supply chain managers, manufacturing and quality assurance teams to avoid the delays associated with sending CAD data back and forth by email like they used to do.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2021-01-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"And as a reminder, fiscal 2021 free cash flow also includes approximately $15 million of restructuring payments related to primarily to the headquarters relocation, as well as to cost actions we took early in fiscal 2020, that’s early last year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2021-01-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"James Heppelmann","x":"In the wake of this strong first quarter, we are increasing our guidance for the year and Kristian will share the details later in the call.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2021-04-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"And also includes approximately $16 million of restructuring payments.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2021-07-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James Heppelmann","x":"Well, I think if you look at any ARR scream at PPC, its growth rate is a function of bookings, churn, but also start dates, backlog, price increases, and so forth.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2021-07-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Approximately $18 million of an unforecasted payment due to a foreign tax dispute and also includes approximately $15 million of restructuring payments.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2021-11-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Tyler Radke","x":"Whether it'd be price increases on the on-time side or maybe initial discounts to get early customers over to the SaaS offering.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2021-11-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Note that our free cash flow for the year included an unforecasted $18 million outflow related to a foreign tax dispute, $15 million in acquisition-related fees, and $15 million in restructuring payments.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2021 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2021-11-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Heppelmann","x":"Given the strength of our financial performance in Fiscal 2021, the restructuring we announced today might come as a surprise to some of you.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2022-01-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Heppelmann","x":"I know that some analysts and investors had voiced concern that the restructuring work we did in late Q4 and throughout Q1 would distract us, but obviously we didn't see that.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2022-01-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Heppelmann","x":"Beta turned to Onshape because of how it enables real time collaboration, allowing the engineering team to work from any location while streamlining their communications during the design process.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2022-04-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"In Q2, free cash flow of $140 million grew 21% year-over-year and included $18 million in restructuring and other related payments.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2022-04-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Still, it's worth mentioning that our costs in Q2 benefited from the restructuring we announced in Q4.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2022-04-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"We're raising our guidance for the second quarter in a row and I think the company has never been in a better position to create shareholder value.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2022-04-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"We're maintaining guidance for fiscal 2022 cash from operations at approximately $430 million as our strong execution and operational discipline are helping us to offset FX headwinds and the Russia exit.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2022-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"So you know like most of our peers, we evaluate pricing typically on an annual – annual basis and you know generally contemplate price increases around the October, kind of November timeframe.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2022-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"That’s been our pattern here for the past – past few years, depending on the overall macro environment and you know competitive environment, we try to take those things into consideration, as we – as we think about price increases.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2022-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"Despite strong FX headwinds and nearly $20 million of restructuring and M&A transaction payments, our free cash flow performance was strong at $112 million, which was ahead of our guidance and up 33% year-over-year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2022-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"Remember that the restructuring we implemented at the end of last fiscal year was designed to drive a more aggressive and efficient SaaS strategy.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2022-07-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"I’m pleased to report that PTC delivered an outstanding third quarter, with top line ARR results and bottom line free cash flow results above our guidance, and we’re raising our guidance for the third time this year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2022-07-27","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"Growth has been accelerating all year, which is why we’re raising our guidance for the third time.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2022-11-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"Price increases provide a helpful tailwind to renewals globally, but the underlying gross churn improvement is what is carried today all year long.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2022-11-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Over the 12 years this model assumes no growth, no price increases nor churn.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2022-11-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"…and up 21% year-over-year despite an approximate $30 million or 700 basis points headwind due to the impact of FX on our operations, including $53 million of payments primarily related to our restructuring from a year ago and fees related to acquisitions, adjusted free cash flow was $468 million.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2022 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2022-11-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"I want to reflect on the margin expansion initiatives we pursued over the past year, including both the restructuring related to our SaaS pivot announced a year ago, and the portfolio resource optimization we discussed on the last call.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2023-02-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"While many notable tech companies are announcing layoffs to come to terms of bloated cost structures, thanks to our proactive actions, we're entering this period of uncertainty with a very lean cost structure and we do not anticipate any need for layoffs or restructuring.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2023-02-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Salesforce just announced a fairly sizable reduction in force.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2023-02-01","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"The summary is that, after posting 15.5% growth in Q1, we remain well positioned to perform against our financial targets and indeed, have raised our guidance accordingly.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2023-02-01","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"On cash flows for fiscal 2023, we raised our guidance.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2023-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"Note that in fiscal '22, we had $41 million of restructuring-related cash outflows for the full year and $18 million in Q2.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2023-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"Excluding the impact of restructuring payments in last year's compare, we still delivered 31% year-over-year free cash flow growth in Q2, driven by a combination of strong ARR growth and higher operating efficiency due to disciplined cost management.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2023-04-26","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"We exceeded our guidance on both metrics in Q2 and are at the midpoint, raising the full year guidance for both metrics.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2023-07-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"So, I would expect that we would see normal kind of normal price increases again, absent some abnormal -- extremely abnormal macro situation.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2023-07-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Note, that we made acquisition and restructuring-related payments of $11 million through the first three quarters of the year, of which $3 million was paid in Q3.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2023-07-26","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Looking at our free cash flow guidance progression, we've been able to raise our guidance every quarter this year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2023 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2023-11-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"Two, we've had more commercial discipline particularly around price increase realization.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2024 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2024-01-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Heppelmann","x":"…like they have some momentum, but I think you remember, too, they put through some fairly nasty price increases, which I think might cover up a little bit what's really happening because the price increases might give them some short-term growth but actually exacerbate the problem that the…","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2024 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2024-01-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Neil Barua","x":"This year, we ought to pass through the $100 million mark on ARR with our ALM segment.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2024 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2024-01-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Neil Barua","x":"They also rearchitect their workflows to streamline inefficiencies and drive collaboration with their manufacturing, quality and service operations.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2024 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2024-01-31","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"As far as the full-year is concerned, again, we are maintaining our full-year guidance, as we start looking at Q2 here.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2024 Q3","e":"ptc","d":"2024-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Neil Barua","x":"A digital thread enables product companies to break down silos, streamline workflows, and achieve interoperability across departments, functions, and systems, a single version of truth.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2024 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2024-11-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Neil Barua","x":"A digital thread enables product companies to breakdown silos, streamline workflows, and achieve interoperability across departments, functions and systems with a single version of the truth.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2024 Q4","e":"ptc","d":"2024-11-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Neil Barua","x":"To be clear, this is not an exercise in cost cutting.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2025 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2025-02-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"On cash flow, we’re guiding the free cash flow of $835 million to $850 million in fiscal 2025, which absorbs the approximately $20 million of cash outflows for severance and consulting fees related to our go-to-market realignment we’ve discussed previously.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2025 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2025-02-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"We’re not calling out a restructuring charge, so all of this will flow through the sales and marketing and cost of revenue lines on our P&L. As we’ve said previously, this is not a cost cutting exercise.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2025 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2025-04-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil Barua","x":"But at the end of the 4 weeks, if this tariff issue does not get resolved or is still unclear the way it currently is to them, we might have to pull back and this might push into Q1 of next year or I might take a smaller chunk.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2025 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2025-04-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Neil Barua","x":"They are clearly going to move forward with digital transformation but they're, right now, trying to figure out where to send excess supply to before the reciprocal tariffs might get taken off the table.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2025 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2025-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jay Vleeschhouwer","x":"So over and above that mid-single digit for your 2 largest businesses, how are you thinking about perhaps pricing or pricing power?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2025 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2025-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jay Vleeschhouwer","x":"Dassault is going to be raising prices 2% to 5% in July.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2025 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2025-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Kristian Talvitie","x":"As a reminder, our fiscal '25 free cash flow guidance of $840 million to $850 million absorbs approximately $19 million of cash outflows for severance and consulting fees related to our go-to-market realignment.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"PTC 2026 Q1","e":"ptc","d":"2026-02-04","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"Neil Barua","x":"In addition to embedding AI in our products, we are building a common AI infrastructure across our product portfolio.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/ptc-ptc-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PTC 2026 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2026-05-06","l":"theater","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Borg","x":"But maybe talk about what you're seeing kind of in that theater specifically?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/ptc-ptc-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PTC 2026 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2026-05-06","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Sameer Kalucha","x":"And the follow-up to that or a similar thing is, do you work with SIs or third-party IT services providers to enable the IT infrastructure modernization that is needed to enable AI use at the customers?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/ptc-ptc-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PTC 2026 Q2","e":"ptc","d":"2026-05-06","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"Neil Barua","x":"Now it is AI foundational infrastructure without all of those versions and the uptick that we're seeing around modernizing that product data foundation, AI won